/-!
# Boundary-point variant: the gadget template chains (data)

For every unit kind the template chain of the boundary-point construction
(boundary
order, from the first vertex after the corridor corner `c1` to the last vertex before `d1`) in
integer template coordinates: the template point `T` is `tmplVBP k = D · T` with
`D = tmplDBP k`.  These are literally the lists `Tmpl.bpGEV`, `Tmpl.bpLEV`, `Tmpl.bpORV`,
`Tmpl.bpInvV` of `BP/Templates/*Data.lean` (same denominators); the bridge lemmas are in
`BP/Assemble/Sep.lean`.  The data is duplicated so that the construction does not depend on the
certificate files.

Also the receivers: `tmplTBP k` lists the template left endpoints `T_τ` of the receivers (index
`τ`; `τ = 0` belongs to the largest working slot), as used by the corridor:

* `ge`: `C = (−2, −21/2)` (`τ = 0`), `W = (−22, −4)`, `B = (−79/2, 0)`;
* `le`: `C = (1/2, −21/2)`, `W = (−22, −3/2)`, `B = (−37, 0)`;
* `orient`: `W = (−22, −4)`, `B = (−79/2, 0)`;
* `inv`: `r_j = (139/10, 1/10)` (`τ = 0`, left-oriented), `r_i = (1/2, 0)` (as in Section 5).

Every receiver (and the weak copy `A` of the addition kinds) lies on the floor of a bay
(`BP/Bay.lean`, `bayRel false` placed at its left end point with scale `1`); `tmplBaysBP k` lists
the bays as (index of the first bay vertex in the chain, left end point).
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace ArtGallery.BP

open ArtGallery.Sec5

